{
  "title": "Costume Contest",
  "logline": "On Halloween, Michael threatens to fire the worst costume as a bit, Dwight abuses his acting title to rig the contest against Andy, and Michael's party dies while Darryl and Pam sit with him.",
  "outline": "A: Michael's Halloween costume contest with a \"fire the worst costume as a bit\" twist; Toby enforces HR rules and Michael makes it personal by firing him too. B: Dwight, self-declared Acting RM, bans Andy's banjo and disqualifies him, then judges himself; Andy and Dwight both lose to Creed. C: Jim and Pam's costume night; Roy forgets again and Jim keeps showing up. Order: cold, A, B, C, A, B, A, C, B, A, C, B, tag.",
  "theme": "Being seen as who you really are, even when you're dressed as someone else.",
  "storySoFar": "Michael still chases Jan's approval; Jan sends maybes and said she is not coming. Stanley's countdown is at 208. Michael's Pretzel Day apology (212 pretzels) is in the break room and Stanley keeps the card. Jim and Pam keep pranking Dwight; her Dwight drawings hang on the crime wall, and Jim bought \"Quality Dessert\" for his apartment. Pam's solo show \"Small Things\" opened and Roy forgot it; Jim showed up and stayed. Roy keeps postponing the wedding and forgets things. Dwight, as self-appointed Acting RM, banned singing by memo and locked Michael out; he gave back the key and kept the title. Andy and Dwight are in an armed truce. Angela and Dwight's secret is unspoken. Kevin's Harvest Cook-Off chili is this Saturday. Toby keeps Michael's folding chair and has filed everything. Michael's Halloween party is in the conference room and is nearly empty.",
  "extras": [],
